@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
skinparam backgroundColor #0D1525
skinparam defaultFontColor #EDF4FF
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #91AED1
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #1A2940
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #91AED1
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #1A2940
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #4A302B
skinparam noteBorderColor #F1AD8A
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45
title HA / failover — conditional decision and verification sequence
actor "Authorized operator" as Op
participant "Operational observation\n(method unselected)" as Obs
participant "Current active service" as Active
participant "Eligible standby\n(if later established)" as Standby
Obs -> Op : suspected failure + evidence/limits
Op -> Obs : confirm affected service, data and external effects
alt no validated standby or no applicable failover plan (current evidence position)
 Op -> Op : record unavailable/degraded scope\nchoose permitted repair or qualified DR assessment
 note over Op,Standby
 No promotion or automatic failover is claimed.
 A second machine alone would not establish HA.
 end note
else later validated standby + authorized failover plan
 Op -> Active : establish exclusive active/writer control\nusing the later selected mechanism
 alt prior writer isolation or candidate consistency not established
  Op -> Op : stop promotion; preserve evidence\navoid conflicting writers / false recovery claim
 else exclusivity and candidate eligibility established
  Op -> Standby : authorize promotion of identified candidate
  Standby --> Op : attributable promotion outcome
  Op -> Standby : check required data, current access\nand critical user operations
  alt required checks pass and routing change confirmed
   Op -> Obs : record scoped usable service and measured interruption/loss
  else outcome unknown or checks fail
   Op -> Op : keep affected use restricted; reconcile\nno blind failback or universal rollback claim
  end
 end
end

legend bottom
Proposed conditional analysis, not an approved runbook or an executed incident.
Standby, replication, routing and failover controls are not established; no numeric RTO/RPO or automatic policy selected.
endlegend
@enduml
